# Deterministic line-endings policy (MO-011).
#
# Why this file exists: governed artifacts in this repository (generic
# source bundles, migration manifests, binding/canonical-projection
# outputs, and every other JSON/JSONL record under knowledge/factory/
# and docs/architecture/) are immutable, byte-hashed lineage records.
# Several generic contracts (see factory_core/canonical/) compute and
# compare SHA-256 over the *raw bytes* of these files, not over
# parsed/normalized JSON. A line-ending change (LF -> CRLF or back)
# changes the byte content without changing the data, which is
# indistinguishable from real tampering to a raw-byte hash check --
# and is exactly what those checks are designed to catch. See
# docs/architecture/MO-011_DETERMINISTIC_LINE_ENDINGS.md for the full
# incident writeup and rationale.
#
# Default: treat text files as text and normalize to LF, both in the
# working tree and in what Git stores, regardless of host OS
# autocrlf settings.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Governed and structured data formats -- must be LF for byte-hash
# stability.
*.json      text eol=lf
*.jsonl     text eol=lf
*.yaml      text eol=lf
*.yml       text eol=lf
*.toml      text eol=lf

# Source and scripting formats.
*.py        text eol=lf
*.ps1       text eol=lf
*.psm1      text eol=lf
*.psd1      text eol=lf
*.sh        text eol=lf
*.bash      text eol=lf

# Documentation.
*.md        text eol=lf
*.txt       text eol=lf
*.rst       text eol=lf

# Windows batch/command files are conventionally CRLF; forcing LF on
# these can break native Windows execution. Explicitly preserved.
*.bat       text eol=crlf
*.cmd       text eol=crlf

# Common binary formats -- never subject to text normalization, diffing,
# or line-ending conversion.
*.pdf       binary
*.png       binary
*.jpg       binary
*.jpeg      binary
*.gif       binary
*.ico       binary
*.zip       binary
*.gz        binary
*.tar       binary
*.7z        binary
*.xlsx      binary
*.xls       binary
*.docx      binary
*.pptx      binary
*.woff      binary
*.woff2     binary
*.ttf       binary
*.otf       binary
